{"name":"Water Tower","hex":"#958f88","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"water tower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large structure consisting of a large tank of water in an elevated position (a large water tank on stilts or on a pedestal), acting as a local reservoir; water is pumped into the tank and fed by gravity to the consumers.","A large metal pipe made to be extended vertically by sections, and used for discharging water upon burning buildings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water_tower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Water tower","blocks":[{"text":"A water tower is an elevated structure supporting a water tank constructed at a height sufficient to pressurize a distribution system for potable water, and to provide emergency storage for fire protection. Water towers often operate in conjunction with underground or surface service reservoirs, which store treated water close to where it will be used. Other types of water towers may only store raw (non-potable) water for fire protection or industrial purposes, and may not necessarily be connected to a public water supply."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Mauston_water_tower_with_cellular_tower_on_top.jpg/330px-Mauston_water_tower_with_cellular_tower_on_top.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_tower"},{"title":"Water Tower (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Water Tower, formerly known as The Water Tower Bucket Boys and Water Tower String Band, is an American bluegrass, old time, and punk band from Los Angeles, California. The band was originally formed in Portland, Oregon in 2005 by Kenny Feinstein and his neighbor, Josh Rabie (fiddle). They put out one album under the name Water Tower String Band and two albums as The Water Tower Bucket Boys, with various line ups, before changing their name to Water Tower in 2012. Rabie left the band in 2013 and Feinstein spent a year recording and putting out a solo album, an acoustic cover of My Bloody Valentine's Loveless called Loveless: Hurts to Love."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Water_Tower_Band_Performing_At_Summer%27s_End_Festival_In_Hailey%2C_Idaho.jpg/330px-Water_Tower_Band_Performing_At_Summer%27s_End_Festival_In_Hailey%2C_Idaho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_Tower_(band)"},{"title":"Water","blocks":[{"text":"Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans. Water is also the fluid of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/H2O_2D_labelled.svg/330px-H2O_2D_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water"},{"title":"Tower","blocks":[{"text":"A tower is a tall structure, taller than it is wide, often by a significant factor. Towers are distinguished from masts by their lack of guy-wires and are therefore, along with tall buildings, self-supporting structures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Tokyo_Sky_Tree_2012.JPG/330px-Tokyo_Sky_Tree_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Water_tower_cellular.webp/500px-Water_tower_cellular.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Water_tower_cellular.webp/1280px-Water_tower_cellular.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Water_tower_cellular.webp/500px-Water_tower_cellular.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_tower_cellular.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Beaumont_Kansas_Water_Tower.jpg/500px-Beaumont_Kansas_Water_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Beaumont_Kansas_Water_Tower.jpg/500px-Beaumont_Kansas_Water_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beaumont St. Louis and San Francisco Railroad Water Tank (1875, restored 2012), Beaumont, Kansas, U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeaumont_Kansas_Water_Tower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Shooters_Hill.JPG/330px-Shooters_Hill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Shooters_Hill.JPG/330px-Shooters_Hill.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shooter's Hill water tower is a local landmark in London, United Kingdom. Water towers are common around London suburbs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShooters_Hill.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Ross_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg/500px-Ross_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Ross_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg/1280px-Ross_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Ross_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg/500px-Ross_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ross Barnett Reservoir water tower in Mississippi, U.S., an example of an older design of water tower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoss_Barnett_Reservoir_water_tower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Utrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg/500px-Utrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Utrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg/1280px-Utrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Utrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg/500px-Utrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A water tower in Utrecht, Netherlands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUtrecht%2C_de_watertoren_aan_het_Lauwerhof_RM514252_foto3_2015-11-01_13.59.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Rooftop_water_towers_on_New_York_apartment_buildings.jpg/500px-Rooftop_water_towers_on_New_York_apartment_buildings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia